    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">For a non-negative integer <var>n</var>, we can iterate the following process:<br><br>1. If <var>n</var> is a palindrome, use <var>n</var> as output <var>r</var> and stop.<br>2. Add reverse(<var>n</var>) to <var>n</var>.<br>3. Go to step 1.<br><br>reverse(<var>n</var>) reverses all digits of <var>n</var>. <const>123456</const> becomes <const>654321</const>. <var>n</var> is a palindrome if <var>n</var> equals reverse(<var>n</var>).<br><br>Given <var>n</var>, output the result <var>r</var> of the iterative process. For the given inputs, the iterative process always terminates.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The integer <var>n</var></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> The result <var>r</var></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">0 &lt;= <var>n</var> &lt; 10^100<br>0 &lt;= <var>r</var> &lt; 10^200</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">27</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">99</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
